# Typesense outputing the search results part 2
created: 2022-12-10, last updated: 2026-06-16, [Read more](https://allotmentandy.github.io/blog/2022-12-10-Typesense-outputing-the-search-results-part-2/)

The second Gotcha, was that the jsonl file had to match the names of the fields in the schema.
...
<?php
require_once __DIR__ . '/vendor/autoload.php';
use Typesense\Client;
// setup the schema
$websiteSchema = [
'name' => 'websites',
...
['name' => 'title', 'type' => 'string'],
['name' => 'description', 'type' => 'string', 'facet' => true],
...
// delete the schema
$client->collections['websites']->delete();
// create the new schema from above in typesense
$client->collections->create($websiteSchema);
// import json file of data
$websitesData = file_get_contents('websites.jsonl');
$client->collections['websites']->documents->import($websitesData, ['action' => 'create']);
// show the result
$result = $client->collections['websites']->retrieve();
var_dump($result);
```
